y\n[@jdx](https://github.com/jdx) in\n[#683](https://github.com/jdx/mise-action/pull/683)\n- replace prettier with oxfmt (#694) by [@jdx](https://github.com/jdx)\nin [#694](https://github.com/jdx/mise-action/pull/694)\n\n<!-- generated by git-cliff -->\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Only version and changelog updates; no runtime code changes in this\ndiff.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Release v5.2.0** — bumps `package.json` from **5.1.2** to **5.2.0**\nand prepends a **5.2.0** `CHANGELOG.md` section (dated 2026-10-16)\ngenerated from prior merged work.\n> \n> The new changelog block documents what ships with this tag: cache\nrebuild every 30 days, retries on throttled cache restore/save, signed\npackslip verification for the mise binary, PATH export via `mise env\n--paths`, monorepo install behavior, docs/CI cache tweaks, and replacing\nPrettier with oxfmt. This diff also corrects the **5.1.2** entry date to\n**2026-10-12**.\n> \n> No application or `dist/` changes appear in this PR; it is version and\nrelease-notes housekeeping only.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n2e65d8f2e6a89728ddad5e704a9bdfd7d0883d9f. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\nCo-authored-by: mise-en-dev <123107610+mise-en-dev@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-16T11:26:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mise-action/commits/9b200bcecbfd6303e69a4a261b2e09e3757440a7","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mise-action/commit/9b200bcecbfd6303e69a4a261b2e09e3757440a7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mise-action/commits/9b200bcecbfd6303e69a4a261b2e09e3757440a7/comments","author":{"login":"jdx","id":216188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b511e8dec14aeeaeeac996371d336fcc5d0a6bed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mise-action/commits/b511e8dec14aeeaeeac996371d336fcc5d0a6bed","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mise-action/commit/b511e8dec14aeeaeeac996371d336fcc5d0a6bed"}]},"status":"ahead","ahead_by":2,"behind_by":0,"total_commits":2,"commits":[{"sha":"720e96afaf7f84d94fc5ff7d76cbee788fa20eed","node_id":"C_kwDOLAFUFNoAKDcyMGU5NmFmYWY3Zjg0ZDk0ZmM1ZmY3ZDc2Y2JlZTc4OGZhMjBlZWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jdx","email":"216188+jdx@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-16T13:38:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-16T13:38:58Z"},"message":"fix: require the signed packslip for mise 2026.9.3 and later (#695)\n\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/jdx/mise-action/trails/55\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\nThe action already checks the downloaded mise binary against the\nrelease's signed packslip, pinned to the `release.yml` workflow at the\nexact tag. But a release with no `packslip.sigstore.json` quietly fell\nback to the weaker minisign and `SHASUMS256` check. So anyone able to\nhide that file could downgrade the verification.\n\nEvery mise release from 2026.9.3 on ships a packslip (2026.9.2 and\nearlier don't). The action now requires one for those releases: if the\nbundle isn't found, the install stops with\n\n```\nmise v2026.10.11 must ship a signed packslip, but https://github.com/jdx/mise/releases/download/v2026.10.11/packslip.sigstore.json was not found\n```\n\nReleases before 2026.9.3 keep the existing fallback to the signed\nchecksums. An explicit `sha256` input still takes precedence, and a\nbundle that fails verification still never falls back.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` (62 pass), including new cases for the version cutoff\nand for a missing packslip on a release that must have one\n- [x] `dist/` rebuilt\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5;\nversion: claude-code_2-1-299_agent.*\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes binary download verification for recent mise releases;\nmis-cutoff or fetch edge cases could block installs, but the change\ncloses a verification downgrade path.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Tightens release integrity verification** so mise **2026.9.3+**\ncannot install without a valid signed `packslip.sigstore.json`.\nPreviously, a missing packslip let verification fall through to\nminisign/`SHASUMS256`, which weakened assurance for releases that are\nsupposed to ship a packslip.\n> \n> `verifyAgainstPackslip` now uses a **`packslipRequired(version)`**\ncutoff: missing bundle on required versions **fails the install** with\nan explicit error; older releases still return `false` so callers can\nuse signed checksums. Invalid or tampered packslips and non-404 fetch\nerrors **still throw** with no fallback. The optional `sha256` input\nbehavior is unchanged.\n> \n> Tests cover the version boundary, required-but-missing packslip, and\nthat failed verification does not downgrade to checksums.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nbf7cfd668cc7bf890a7c7cb68770ced2c3487390. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Release verification now requires a packslip for versions from\n2026.9.3 onward. If the required packslip is missing, verification\nfails.\n* Older releases can still be verified using minisign checksums when no\npackslip is available.\n* Version strings that do not follow the expected three-part numeric\nformat are treated as requiring a packslip.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e6e9847ad139c9b1c321cb461f2659a5a95f284","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mise-action/git/trees/0e6e9847ad139c9b1c321cb461f2659a5a95f284"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mise-action/git/commits/720e96afaf7f84d94fc5ff7d76cbee788fa20eed","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"val