hecksums. An explicit `sha256` input still takes precedence, and a\nbundle that fails verification still never falls back.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` (62 pass), including new cases for the version cutoff\nand for a missing packslip on a release that must have one\n- [x] `dist/` rebuilt\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n*AI-assisted — Tool: Claude Code; model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5;\nversion: claude-code_2-1-299_agent.*\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes binary download verification for recent mise releases;\nmis-cutoff or fetch edge cases could block installs, but the change\ncloses a verification downgrade path.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Tightens release integrity verification** so mise **2026.9.3+**\ncannot install without a valid signed `packslip.sigstore.json`.\nPreviously, a missing packslip let verification fall through to\nminisign/`SHASUMS256`, which weakened assurance for releases that are\nsupposed to ship a packslip.\n> \n> `verifyAgainstPackslip` now uses a **`packslipRequired(version)`**\ncutoff: missing bundle on required versions **fails the install** with\nan explicit error; older releases still return `false` so callers can\nuse signed checksums. Invalid or tampered packslips and non-404 fetch\nerrors **still throw** with no fallback. The optional `sha256` input\nbehavior is unchanged.\n> \n> Tests cover the version boundary, required-but-missing packslip, and\nthat failed verification does not downgrade to checksums.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nbf7cfd668cc7bf890a7c7cb68770ced2c3487390. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n* Release verification now requires a packslip for versions from\n2026.9.3 onward. If the required packslip is missing, verification\nfails.\n* Older releases can still be verified using minisign checksums when no\npackslip is available.\n* Version strings that do not follow the expected three-part numeric\nformat are treated as requiring a packslip.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-16T13:38:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mise-action/commits/720e96afaf7f84d94fc5ff7d76cbee788fa20eed","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx/mise-action/commit/720e96afaf7f84d94fc5ff7d76cbee788fa20eed","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jdx/mise-action/commits/720e96afaf7f84d94fc5ff7d76cbee788fa20eed/comments","author":{"login":"jdx","id":216188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjE4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx","html_url":"https://github.com/jdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","f